-- title:
--   Twisted elliptic norm classes re-indexed by scalars modulo norms
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension of fields and $\sigma$ a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ with the property that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$. Let $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ lie in the elliptic cell, i.e. the characteristic polynomial of the underlying matrix of $\gamma_0$ has no root in $K$. Here $\sigma$-conjugacy is the relation $\delta_2 = h^{-1}\delta_1\,\sigma(h)$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, `SigmaConjClasses.mk` sends $\delta$ to its $\sigma$-conjugacy class, and `normClassMap` sends such a class to the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$-conjugacy class of a $K$-rational representative of the $\sigma$-norm of $\delta$. Let $R_L \subseteq \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ be a set such that (i) no two of its elements are related by $\delta_2 = u\,(h^{-1}\delta_1\,\sigma(h))$ with $u \in L^\times$ scalar and $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, and (ii) every $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ whose norm class is that of $a\gamma_0$ for some $a \in K^\times$ has the form $u\,(h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(h))$ for some $\delta_0 \in R_L$, $u \in L^\times$, $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$. Let $A : \mathrm{GL}_2(L) \to K^\times$ be such that for every $\delta_0 \in R_L$ whose norm class is that of some $a\gamma_0$, that norm class is the class of $A(\delta_0)\gamma_0$. Let $T \subseteq K^\times$ be such that every $a \in K^\times$ admits a unique $t$ with $t \in T$ and $a = t\,N_{L/K}(b)$ for some $b \in L^\times$. Let $\Phi : K^\times \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfy $\Phi(as) = \Phi(a)$ whenever $s\gamma_0 = h^{-1}\gamma_0 h$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, $\Phi(a\,N_{L/K}(b)) = \Phi(a)$ for all $b \in L^\times$, and $\Phi(a) = 0$ whenever the class of $a\gamma_0$ is not in the range of `normClassMap`. Then the finsum over $\delta_0$ in the intersection of $R_L$ with the set of $\delta$ whose norm class is that of $a\gamma_0$ for some $a \in K^\times$, of $e_L(\delta_0)^{-1}\,\Phi(A(\delta_0))$, equals the finsum over $t \in T$ of $e_K^{-1}\,\Phi(t)$. Here $e_L(\delta_0)$ is the number of classes in $L^\times$ modulo the image of $u \mapsto \sigma(u)u^{-1}$ that contain some $u$ with $u\delta_0 = h^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(h)$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, and $e_K$ is the number of $a \in K^\times$ with $a\gamma_0 = h^{-1}\gamma_0 h$ for some $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K)$, both read as natural cardinalities (hence $0$, with inverse $0$ in $\mathbb{C}$, when infinite).
--
--   This is the combinatorial heart of Langlands' comparison, for a cyclic extension $L/K$, of the elliptic term of the trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ with the $\sigma$-elliptic term of the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}_2(L)$: the $\sigma$-conjugacy classes with norm class a scalar multiple of a fixed elliptic class, weighted by the twisted multiplicities, are matched with the scalars modulo norms, weighted by the untwisted multiplicity. It is stated for an arbitrary class function $\Phi$ satisfying the relevant invariances, and is used in the base-change identity [`AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_forall_perClass`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.finsum_sigmaCentralizerDomain_ellipticNorm_eq_mul_sum_finsum_centralizerDomain_elliptic_of_forall_perClass); its proof cites the injectivity of the norm map on $\sigma$-classes with a given elliptic norm class.
